{:edb/db-before-t 2523 :edb/db-after-t 2524 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535836 50 #inst "2026-10-09T08:29:52.210Z" 13194139535836 true] [17592186175912 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369224 13194139535836 true] [17592186175912 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369231 13194139535836 true] [17592186175949 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369238 13194139535836 true] [17592186175949 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369245 13194139535836 true] [17592186176235 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535836 true] [17592186176235 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/8ba69d7bfe8dd363288bbf86661172004b21143f02c70260da0c184f066a7c12.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y)=⟨{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{3},\\,y{e}^{y+1}+x⟩,$ which of the following is equivalent to ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr\\,?$" 13194139535836 true] [17592186176235 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3627/Source/Images/q-125719.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Given that $F(x, y) = ⟨x^{2}\\cos x + y^{3}, ye^{y + 1} + x⟩$, which of the following is equivalent to $∮_(C)F \\cdot dr$?" 13194139535836 false] [17592186176235 1145 "First, notice that we can rewrite our integral as \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{3})\\,dx+(y{e}^{y+1}+x)\\,dy.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/3b90abecc774b5ba5dcee19385fef38b14206d2c31c3b6cba38216bfa9957448.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{3}$ and $Q(x,y)=y{e}^{y+1}+x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{3})\\,dx-(y{e}^{y+1}+x)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(1-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(1-3\\cdot {r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-3{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369224 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369225 13194139535836 true] [17592186369224 1089 "q-126686" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369224 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535836 true] [17592186369224 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/e44543ad51864a7db6b8e80b5c560a1ac773a7537573014f737451af4d1209a7.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}(x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dy\\,?\n$$" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369224 1113 #uuid "b97bdd87-b8e7-5fa0-84d3-dcb91e945069" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369224 1145 "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/d8ee02b2b7282349604dc6305c0b2be796cfdbd2937e06d089e660683a5785ad.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-(2xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 5,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}2{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369226 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369227 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369228 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369229 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369230 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1041 "selection" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369230 13194139535836 true] [17592186369225 1110 #uuid "40a04b29-f889-5a24-a38e-1159cf6cd53d" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369226 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369226 1111 #uuid "daab7196-75ee-5175-81bb-5018c5a64555" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369227 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369227 1111 #uuid "d6115739-19d5-52c3-84c7-d2e689185b43" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369228 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369228 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369228 1111 #uuid "9980c91b-cb47-5f99-9c24-10cd17ba48e1" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369229 1034 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369229 1111 #uuid "229a0908-ea5e-5643-9b41-5b5742e54e00" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369230 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369230 1111 #uuid "dfd08c1d-7fcb-5467-8ecf-dc4116090e1d" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369231 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369232 13194139535836 true] [17592186369231 1089 "q-126687" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369231 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535836 true] [17592186369231 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/e49bde14ba6097dfc7b153d5b93c2be2462b141a37357bfff826c852fc1136eb.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}(2-xy+2{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+xy)\\,dy\\,?\n$$" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369231 1113 #uuid "208a1083-56ad-5853-aae0-e9bfc216a1b0" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369231 1145 "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/8b3c794f11c0a9be558e66c1c7a4ae4cd996037bbd6e491eefaa1a2e9000c596.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)=2-xy+2{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}+xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-x+4y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x+y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(2-xy+2{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+xy)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x+y-(-x+4y))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3x-3y)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 8,\\,-\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(3x-3y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}3{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369233 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369234 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369235 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369236 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369237 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1041 "selection" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369233 13194139535836 true] [17592186369232 1110 #uuid "90afa4b1-b9f6-514b-a164-257986be804d" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369233 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}3{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369233 1111 #uuid "b13f0e98-1625-5fc5-9463-5ed239808695" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369234 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369234 1111 #uuid "11b922f4-d37a-5953-933c-664e05647d7e" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369235 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}2{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369235 1111 #uuid "c18ce837-d0d2-5ba2-8bdf-67e133e2fb1a" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369236 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}3{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369236 1111 #uuid "aa6ac347-f7e3-5f27-925b-11f80acce604" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369237 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}r(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369237 1111 #uuid "a6036a58-5415-507a-b060-5e0fcdbaf879" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369238 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369239 13194139535836 true] [17592186369238 1089 "q-126756" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369238 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535836 true] [17592186369238 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/d675e8d06f2037531a2eec3a7e48374bb0d2e5cb59adfee0cbee5ce3a23add67.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∮}_{C}({e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y)dx+({e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2})\\,dy,$ where the path $C$ is shown above." 13194139535836 true] [17592186369238 1113 #uuid "44f0dbe7-0e3a-5de7-ab4d-8d28f09f8e89" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369238 1145 "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/96998e4a17d20459622486970518a677309b23fd936c993d8c97dcf0d65a9a29.png)\n\n \n\nNow, since \n\n$$\nP(x,y)={e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y,\\,Q(x,y)={e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2},\n$$\n\n we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y)dx+({e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2{y}^{2}-(-2{x}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({y}^{2}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFinally, we can calculate our double integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2({y}^{2}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2({r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{r}^{3}({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\frac{81}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}[\\theta ]_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{81\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369240 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369241 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369242 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369243 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369244 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1041 "selection" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369244 13194139535836 true] [17592186369239 1110 #uuid "093ca155-1c15-5460-a43a-aabbb97c8b18" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369240 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369240 1111 #uuid "56f8af69-44dc-5e3f-a4ae-eb66ec35dc80" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369241 1034 "\\frac{27\\pi }{2}" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369241 1111 #uuid "92045d9d-3bfd-5000-a8a4-1ebec6775423" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369242 1034 "\\frac{27\\pi }{4}" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369242 1111 #uuid "80522476-fae7-5579-8543-aeb55dcd8c5c" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369243 1034 "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369243 1111 #uuid "645ddde7-ebed-59a9-9543-6eac390d38aa" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369244 1034 "\\frac{81\\pi }{4}" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369244 1111 #uuid "eb82bb64-7e72-5ce3-bd7e-f0f588aef175" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369245 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369246 13194139535836 true] [17592186369245 1089 "q-126758" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369245 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535836 true] [17592186369245 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/bcdc0f59fa284c2b1f1621e7de057ef6f0e084d2eca6732fbc5eae3f74ede113.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∮}_{C}(\\sqrt{5+x}-3{x}^{2}y)dx+({e}^{-{y}^{2}}+3x{y}^{2})\\,dy,$ where the path $C$ is shown above." 13194139535836 true] [17592186369245 1113 #uuid "885d7e93-ddfe-5056-8a1a-3e87c6540035" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369245 1145 "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/6273034b38059d3d49b2a29c91052c290151b4a29073f1c925172dd1c4c2bf72.png)\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\sqrt{5+x}-3{x}^{2}y,\\,Q(x,y)={e}^{-{y}^{2}}+3x{y}^{2},\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-3{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(\\sqrt{5+x}-3{x}^{2}y)dx+({e}^{-{y}^{2}}+x{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3{y}^{2}-(-3{x}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,2\\le r\\le 4,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFinally, we can calculate our double integral, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}3({r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}3{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]}_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}60\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =180[\\theta ]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =180\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =90\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369247 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369248 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369249 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369250 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369251 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1041 "selection" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369249 13194139535836 true] [17592186369246 1110 #uuid "3835ccf8-f8a6-5e2c-bc0d-83549731713d" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369247 1034 "\\frac{90\\pi }{4}" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369247 1111 #uuid "9879f38c-33ca-5de8-8de2-56c97bbc7e10" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369248 1034 "15\\pi " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535836 true] [17592186369248 1111 #uuid "ff94dc02-10ca-5e75-a954-d2579ea25d0f" 13194139535836 true] [17592186369249 1034 "90\\pi " 13194139535836 true] [17592186369249 1103 #edb/ref 17